dav-ext: with LOCK (a dav_ext_lock_zone), the DAV header of the answer to OPTIONS
names the classes 1 and 2, "DAV: 1,2", not "2" alone: RFC 4918 (18.2) wants a class 2
resource to give at least "1" and "2", as Apache mod_dav does. Without a lock zone it
stays "DAV: 1". https://github.com/arut/nginx-dav-ext-module/pull/46 (Alexey Lubimov,
20.08.2019), as Alpine carries it (main/nginx, nginx-dav-ext-module~dav-class-1-2.patch);
aZ, 18.11.2026: LOCK may come.

--- src/ngx_http_dav_ext_module.c.orig
+++ src/ngx_http_dav_ext_module.c
@@ -502,8 +502,16 @@
         }
 
         ngx_str_set(&h->key, "DAV");
-        h->value.len = 1;
-        h->value.data = (u_char *) (dlcf->shm_zone ? "2" : "1");
+
+        if (dlcf->shm_zone) {
+            h->value.len = 3;
+            h->value.data = (u_char *) "1,2";
+
+        } else {
+            h->value.len = 1;
+            h->value.data = (u_char *) "1";
+        }
+
         h->hash = 1;
 
         h = ngx_list_push(&r->headers_out.headers);
